Z||000005||mrfixit58||10-04-2001||07:35 AM||||If the car is in an impound lot, the only investment the lot has into it is the towing fee. If he is willing to sell it to you, he will probably take $100-$300 for it. If your offer is even slightly more than the local junk yard would offer he will make more money. <P>The other obstacle is the title... or lack there of. Most likely, the two company doesn't have one for it. If you want to get this car on the street you might better check with your local tag office to see what is involved in obtaining a rebuilt title. That process alone will determine if the car is destined to be a parts car or a street car.<P>Good Luck,<P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||4
